{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1098788-why-don-t-certain-powers-have-contested-dice-rolls","id":1098788,"title":"Why don't certain powers have contested dice rolls?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-31T08:53:52-07:00","id":1098788,"title":"Why don't certain powers have contested dice rolls?","content":"Certain knacks just don't seem to have limitations/downsides.<br /> i.e. There is no limitation on using them against higher legend opponents and no way for opponents to resist the effects.<br /> I mean, there is no rule to say that a hero level Scion can't use Overt Order or Serpent's Gaze on a God, or that it won;t work.<br /> <br /> I tried creating my own limitations, but my players bitched that it wasn't how it was written in the books.<br /> I don't want to be the GM that just says ''screw the rules, I'm changing everything'', but a lot of knacks just seem unbalanced.<br /> <br /> <br /> For example: <span style=\"color:#4E4F43\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Overt Order</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#4E4F43\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes, the direct method is more effective than the cleverest of intricate schemes. With this Knack, a Scion barks out a command that the target must obey. Doing so costs one Willpower, and the command must be one the Scion can give and the victim can perform in a single action. \u201cFreeze!\u201d is acceptable, as is, \u201cDon\u2019t shoot!\u201d or, \u201cShoot him!\u201d Ordering someone to go home and shoot his wife won\u2019t work because doing so would take longer than a single action. A victim of this Knack can interpret the command loosely to make it not directly suicidal, but not if all he\u2019s trying to do is keep out of trouble. For example, if a victim draws a gun and the Scion commands him to shoot himself, the victim can shoot himself in the hand or the foot rather than blowing his own brains out. Same thing goes if a Scion uses this Knack at a seedy pool hall to command a smarmy drug dealer to pick a \ufb01ght with a burly ex-con at the next table. The dealer might reasonably believe that the ex-con could kill him, but he still can\u2019t weasel out of the command. He doesn\u2019t have to walk up and take a swing at the guy, but he still has to do something, such as singing out a racial slur or throwing a beer bottle at the guy\u2019s girlfriend. The dealer can cheese it immediately, but he\u2019s still got to pick the \ufb01ght \ufb01rst.<br /> <br /> Here we have an ability with no real limitation. In combat, player A uses Overt Order on Big Bad Monster to freeze him in his tracks, letting the rest of the party get a round of free hits in. As when a character is rendered inactive, their DV drops to 0.<br /> This means my players just kill whatever big threat is in front of them in 2 or 3 rounds of combat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Serpent\u2019s Gaze</b><br /> <br /> When the Scion spends a point of Legend, the person whom she\u2019s trying to affect locks eyes with her and is unable to look away. For combat purposes, the victim is rendered Inactive until the Scion breaks eye contact. The Scion can still act, but she must take a second action in order to do so, maintaining eye contact as a diceless action. (As a result, she suffers a -2 penalty for any other action she takes.) This Knack works equally well whether the Scion\u2019s Epic Appearance involves beauty or its opposite. Characters of lesser Legend are unable to break the Scion\u2019s gaze on their own, but those with an equal or greater Legend are not so vulnerable. After the Scion using the Knack takes one full action, the equal- or higher-Legend victim may spend a point of Willpower to negate the effect. In so doing, he remains immune to the effect from the same Scion for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> Similar thing here, enemy is rendered inactive, dropping his DV to zero, allowing for a whole round of free hits.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> There seem to be a lot of knacks like this, that don't have limitations/downsides.<br /> \u200bIs this normal? Am I just interpreting this wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13518,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13518-thebeastisback2007","user":"thebeastisback2007","date":". 05-31-2017, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13518-thebeastisback2007","name":"thebeastisback2007","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T09:19:23-07:00","id":1098795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thebeastisback2007</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1098788-why-don-t-certain-powers-have-contested-dice-rolls#post1098788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certain knacks just don't seem to have limitations/downsides.<br /> i.e. There is no limitation on using them against higher legend opponents and no way for opponents to resist the effects.<br /> I mean, there is no rule to say that a hero level Scion can't use Overt Order or Serpent's Gaze on a God, or that it won;t work.<br /> <br /> I tried creating my own limitations, but my players bitched that it wasn't how it was written in the books.<br /> I don't want to be the GM that just says ''screw the rules, I'm changing everything'', but a lot of knacks just seem unbalanced.<br /> <br /> There seem to be a lot of knacks like this, that don't have limitations/downsides.<br /> \u200bIs this normal? Am I just interpreting this wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW Scion 1e is really, <i>really</i> broken. Overt Order and Serpent's Gaze being the very top of the iceberg. Stacking Animal Aspect buffed Do Not Want with RAW Untouchable Opponent leaves your DDV so high it is impossible to hit without looping Animal Aspect to buff Animal Aspect.<br /> <br /> Screwing the rules and changing everything is pretty common, with various ST's screwing the rules to different degrees. For this problem you are seeing here, the most common fix is instituting something like a Mental DV, normally based on Wits or Intelligence. If you are looking for a full collection of such houserules, check <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/home\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> out.<br /> <br /> I will say however that there is great stories in Heroic Scions messing with Gods. Not all Gods are amazingly resilient in the social department. Scions enthralling Deities or even Titans to adoring them can make a fun, if exceptionally dangerous for the Scion, story. Selene is a good example of that. The game does benefit from... some big fixes though.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, as the ST you have the final call. Your players may not realize the degree to which the game is broken, and you might want to have a frank discussion with them about adopting one of the houserule systems to make the game functional. The game can also be simplified a bunch, and open up far more possibilities for capable characters if you change from RAW as well if that might entice them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T06:52:18-07:00","id":1099136,"title":"","content":"Completely agree with everything Watcher said. Scion 1st Ed, though an amazing and superfun game, it was pure nonsense when it came to the rules. I do have, however, one suggestion to make, taking into account those players of yours: face them against an enemy group composed by the usual 3-4 bulking, resilient monsters, and another 3-4 lean creatures... all of them possesing Overt Order and Serpent's Gaze. Play by their rules, make them experience the <b><i>fun</i></b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}